2,40) Refer to the production possibilities frontier in Figure 2.1.3. The opportunity cost of moving from C to B will be,A) greater than moving from D to C but less than moving from B to A.,B) less than moving from D to C but greater than moving from B to A.,C) the same as moving from D to C or moving from B to A.,D) greater than moving either from D to C or from B to A.,E) neither greater than moving from D to C nor moving from B to A.,A,Production Possibilities and Opportunity Cost,False
