7,1) Economists usually agree with which of the following arguments that favour protectionism?,A) the competition with cheap foreign labour defence,B) the job protection defence,C) the dumping defence,D) the infant-industry defence,E) None of the above. Economists generally agree that arguments in favor of protection are flawed.,E,The Case Against Protection,False
7,2) Which of the following are valid reasons advanced by almost all economists? Protection,A) saves jobs.,B) prevents rich countries from exploiting developing countries.,C) is a good way for governments in developed nations to raise revenue.,D) penalizes lax environmental standards.,E) Economists would not support any of the above reasons.,E,The Case Against Protection,False
