13,18) Consumer surplus is,A) positive in the case of a monopolist practicing perfect price discrimination.,B) equal to price minus marginal cost.,C) less in the case of a single-price monopoly than in the case of a perfectly competitive industry.,D) zero for a single-price monopolist.,E) greater in a single-price monopoly than in a perfectly competitive industry.,C,Single-Price Monopoly and Competition Compared,False
