13,"20) In comparison to a perfectly competitive industry, a single-price monopolist with the same costs creates a ________ consumer surplus and makes ________ economic profit.",A) smaller; a larger,B) smaller; a smaller,C) larger; a larger,D) larger; a smaller,E) smaller; the same,A,Single-Price Monopoly and Competition Compared,False
13,21) Rent seeking is best defined as attempts,A) by landlords to get tenants.,B) to achieve monopoly power and the resulting economic profit.,C) by individuals to avoid paying taxes.,D) by owners of a monopoly to sell the firm.,E) none of the above.,B,Single-Price Monopoly and Competition Compared,False
