13,5) A monopolist under marginal cost pricing has an incentive to,A) inflate costs.,B) produce more than the efficient quantity of output.,C) produce less than the efficient quantity of output.,D) maximize consumer surplus.,E) produce the efficient quantity of output.,E,Monopoly Regulation,False
13,6) Which one of the following is most likely to be a natural monopoly?,A) sandwich shops,B) printing services,C) welding services,D) automotive service,E) electric utilities,E,Monopoly Regulation,False
