17,"30) According to public choice theory, a voter will tend to be well informed if the issue in question",A) is complicated and difficult to understand.,B) affects everyone a little.,C) is of special interest to a small group to which the voter does not belong.,D) has a large direct effect on the voter.,E) is important even if it does not directly affect the voter.,D,Public Goods and the Free-Rider Problem,False
