18,1) The four factors of production are,"A) productive factors, neutral factors, entrepreneurial factors, and nonproductive factors.","B) men, women, animals, and children.","C) labour, capital, entrepreneurship, and land.","D) machines, factories, buildings, and farms.","E) labour, money, profits, and land.",C,The Anatomy of Factor Markets,False
