18,5) What is the most an investor would be willing to pay for a stock that will pay $210 next year and nothing before or after?,A) $200 regardless of the interest rate.,B) $200 if the interest rate is 5 percent per year.,C) $190.91 if the interest rate is 10 percent per year.,D) B and C.,E) None of the above.,D,Mathematical Note: Present Value and Discounting,False
18,6) The present value of a future payment of money will be higher the,A) higher the interest rate or the further in the future the payment.,B) lower the interest rate or the further in the future the payment.,C) higher the interest rate or the nearer the date of the future payment.,D) lower the interest rate or the nearer the date of the future payment.,"E) lower the interest rate, independent of the date of the future payment.",D,Mathematical Note: Present Value and Discounting,False
18,7) The present value of a future payment of money will be lower the,A) higher the interest rate or the further in the future the payment.,B) lower the interest rate or the further in the future the payment.,C) higher the interest rate or the nearer the date of the future payment.,D) lower the interest rate or the nearer the date of the future payment.,"E) lower the interest rate, independent of the date of the future payment.",A,Mathematical Note: Present Value and Discounting,False
