19,"36) In an economy in 2000, 3 million people had full-time managerial and professional jobs that paid an average of $800 a week. At the same time, 1 million people had full-time sales positions that paid an average of $530 a week. Managers and professionals are paid more than salespeople because ________.",A) the supply curve of managers and professionals lies above that of salespeople,B) the demand curve for managers and professionals lies above that of salespeople,C) managers and professionals have a a higher value of marginal product,D) the typical manager or professional has incurred a higher cost of education,E) all of the above,E,The Sources of Economic Inequality,False
