23,"18) If the Ricardo-Barro effect occurs, a government budget deficit raises the equilibrium real interest rate by ________ and decreases the equilibrium quantity of investment by ________ if the Ricardo-Barro effect is absent.",A) more; more than,B) more; less than,C) less; more than,D) less; less than,E) the same amount; the same amount as,D,Government in the Market for Loanable Funds,False
23,19) A decrease in the government budget deficit decreases the ________ loanable funds and an increase in the government budget surplus increases the ________ loanable funds.,A) demand for; demand for,B) demand for; supply of,C) supply of; demand for,D) supply of; supply of,E) demand for loanable funds and the supply of; supply of loanable funds and the demand for,B,Government in the Market for Loanable Funds,False
23,"20) Refer to Table 23.3.1. Table 23.3.1 shows the market for loanable funds in Northland. The government budget is balanced. If the government moves from a balanced budget to a surplus of $20 billion, the new equilibrium has a real interest rate of ________ and quantity of loanable funds traded equal to ________.",A) 6.5%; $110 billion,B) 6.5%; $90 billion,C) 5.5%; $90 billion,D) 5.5%; $110 billion,E) 6%; $120 billion,D,Government in the Market for Loanable Funds,False
