31,5) A country,A) imports those goods in which it has a comparative advantage.,B) exports those goods in which it has a comparative advantage.,C) imports goods produced in countries with lower wage rates.,D) exports goods produced by domestic industries with low wages relative to its trading partners.,E) B and D are correct.,B,How Global Markets Work,False
