31,"19) A country opens up to trade. In an import industry,",A) domestic producers lose and domestic consumers gain.,B) domestic consumers lose and domestic producers gain.,C) the government loses and domestic consumers gain.,D) domestic producers lose and the government gains.,E) none of the above.,A,"Winners, Losers and the Net Gain from Trade",False
31,20) Refer to Table 31.1.2. The table shows a country's demand and supply schedules. At what world price would the country import?,A) at exactly $8 a unit,B) any price above $8 a unit,C) a price of $10 a unit,D) a price of $20 a unit,E) a price below $8 a unit,E,"Winners, Losers and the Net Gain from Trade",False
